--TEST--
Every row of the precedence table that can group two ways groups the way its associativity column says — `-`, `%`, `>>` and `.` to the left, `**`, the ternary and the assignment to the right — and each row that the two groupings disagree on also states the grouping it does not have, `rule:types/arithmetic`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/precedence-and-associativity
// Associativity decides the order when two operators of the same strength
// meet. Each row below states both halves: the grouping the table gives it,
// and the grouping it does not have. A row that only stated the first would
// pass on an operator that groups the other way and happens to agree.

uint $groupedAsWritten = 0;
uint $differFromTheOther = 0;

// `-` groups to the left: (1 - 2) - 3 is -4, and 1 - (2 - 3) is 2.
if (1 - 2 - 3 == (1 - 2) - 3) { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }
if (1 - 2 - 3 != 1 - (2 - 3)) { $differFromTheOther = $differFromTheOther + 1; }

// `%` groups to the left: (10 % 4) % 3 is 2, and 10 % (4 % 3) is 0.
if (10 % 4 % 3 == (10 % 4) % 3) { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }
if (10 % 4 % 3 != 10 % (4 % 3)) { $differFromTheOther = $differFromTheOther + 1; }

// `>>` groups to the left: (16 >> 2) >> 2 is 1, and 16 >> (2 >> 2) is 16.
if (16 >> 2 >> 2 == (16 >> 2) >> 2) { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }
if (16 >> 2 >> 2 != 16 >> (2 >> 2)) { $differFromTheOther = $differFromTheOther + 1; }

// `.` groups to the left, and the two groupings agree, so this row states
// only the grouping the table gives it.
if ("a" . "b" . "c" == ("a" . "b") . "c") { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }

// `**` groups to the right: 2 ** (3 ** 2) is 512, and (2 ** 3) ** 2 is 64.
if (2 ** 3 ** 2 == 2 ** (3 ** 2)) { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }
if (2 ** 3 ** 2 != (2 ** 3) ** 2) { $differFromTheOther = $differFromTheOther + 1; }

// The ternary groups to the right: the second `?` belongs to the `:` before
// it, so this is 2 and not 1.
int $choice = false ? 1 : true ? 2 : 3;
if ($choice == (false ? 1 : (true ? 2 : 3))) { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }
if ($choice != 1) { $differFromTheOther = $differFromTheOther + 1; }

// The assignment groups to the right: the value is worked out once and every
// variable on the way takes it.
int $first = 0;
int $second = 0;
$first = $second = 5 + 2;
if ($first == 7 && $second == 7) { $groupedAsWritten = $groupedAsWritten + 1; }

echo "grouped as the table says: ", $groupedAsWritten, " of 7\n";
echo "rows that differ from the other grouping: ", $differFromTheOther, " of 5\n";
--EXPECT--
grouped as the table says: 7 of 7
rows that differ from the other grouping: 5 of 5
